arch-neutral suite on x86-64 (native)
facts (allowed to differ):
  byte order         little-endian
  sizeof(void*)      8, sizeof(long) 8
  plain char is      signed
  page size          4096 (sysconf)
  64-bit atomics     always lock-free
  max_align_t        16 bytes
tests (must pass everywhere):
  ok    explicit little-endian read of an ext2 magic
  ok    explicit big-endian read of a DTB magic
  ok    network-order and on-disk 32-bit fields
  ok    page arithmetic with the page size as a parameter (4, 16, 64 KiB)
  ok    byte classification through unsigned char
  ok    release/acquire message passing, 20000 rounds
  ok    atomic fetch_add from 4 threads
  ok    pointers stored only in uintptr_t
